-- Blizzard's WoW: Forever hotfix list (the forum post at `source`), in short,
-- for the Settings page's Game hotfixes link (UI/Hotfixes.lua). Written by
-- hand, every entry in NeedRoll's own words: Blizzard's text is theirs and is
-- never copied here. English data, like the rest of the data's notes; the
-- page's own labels are translated.
--
-- tools/hotfixes.py compares it with the post (see tools/README.md). Each
-- entry's `key` names the post's bullet it sums up (a hash of its day, topic
-- and Blizzard's wording), so a new or reworded bullet shows up as new.
-- `topic` is Blizzard's section and subsections. `note = true` marks a
-- developers' note on the entry above it. `removed` is the day the bullet
-- left Blizzard's list: the page shows it struck through, and it is never
-- deleted, so what was changed and then reverted stays on record.
-- One entry per line: the tool reads and edits them line by line.
